# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF. Without this file git has no opinion about what a
# working tree should get, so a WSL checkout on /mnt/c materialises CRLF and
# every file it touches reports as modified with no content change — 195 of
# them, for months, hiding real changes in the noise and blocking any
# fast-forward that lands on one.
#
# Prettier already enforces `endOfLine: "lf"` for this repo. This makes git
# agree with it, in every checkout, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-for-byte, never filtered.
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
